**`ZenEnhancement::StillImageTune` recipe v1 — measured on a 42-image
k-means-diverse imazen-26 subset.** The bundle = C's tune-IQ overrides
(`apply_tune_overrides`: QM on + still levels, sharpness 7, variance boost
strength 3 / curve 2, `max_tx_size` 32 at qp<=45, `screen_content_mode = 3`)
verbatim. The recipe's only delta vs `with_tune(Iq)`: bundle-covered knobs
are snapshotted first and caller-set values survive, so with no caller
extras the emitted stream is byte-identical to plain tune IQ.

date:   2026-09-19 (analysis corrected same-day — see §4)
host:   r7900x — AMD Ryzen 9 7900X (Zen 4), no hw perf counters
        (perf_event_paranoid=4) — wall clock + child cpu via getrusage,
        spawn overhead included identically in every arm.
port:   `ba8d35e52` + working tree (SvtTune enum, with_tune,
        StillImageTune, SB128+VB re-derivation fix). C reference `3115c0c1b`.
rustc:  1.98.1
data:   benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_round1_2026-09-19.tsv (1512 cells)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_round2_2026-09-19.tsv (756 cells)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_zones_2026-09-19.tsv (4410 cells)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_oct_2026-09-19.tsv (3024 cells)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_backfill_2026-09-19.tsv (6930 cells)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_s46_2026-09-19.tsv (1008 cells)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_subset_2026-09-19.tsv (42 images)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_sweep_*.py (harnesses)

========================= 1. SUBSET =========================

42 images, 21 top-level classes, exactly 2 per class — the class's two
largest k-means clusters' representatives from
`imazen-26-png-v3/manifests/kmeans_k300_representatives.tsv` where present,
else the next distinct representative of that class. Git-LFS materialized
(`git lfs pull`); all 42 verified PNG-signatured, not pointer stubs.

Protocol per cell: `identity_run "crop:<png>" 512 512 <qp> <preset> <out>`
plus the arm's env — the encoder's own `crop:` path center-crops to 512²
and converts RGB→I420 with its integer BT.601-limited transform;
`<out>.yuv` records the exact samples encoded. Then `aomdec -o <out>.y4m`,
y4m→I420 (the parser skips the per-frame `FRAME\n` marker — see §4),
inverse BT.601 to PNG, `fast-ssim2-cli image <src.png> <dec.png>`.
wall_ms is whole-process wall clock; cpu_ms is rusage user+sys of the
child. qp ∈ {20, 32, 44}; presets −1,0,1,2,4,6,8,10,12; all-intra.

16380 cells total across the campaign; every stream aomdec-decoded —
0 decode errors after the SB128+VB fix (§3).

========================= 2. HEADLINE — per-speed-zone curve =================

BD-rate vs `t1` (default tune), ssim2 quality axis, log-rate piecewise
interpolation over the qp{20,32,44} curve, n=42 images per cell.
Negative = fewer bytes at equal quality. Median / [p25,p75]:

  preset   t2(SSIM)        t3(IQ)           t4(MS-SSIM)     st(bundle)
   -1      -1.5 [-3.3,-0.2] -4.2 [-10.1,+3.6] -5.0 [-9.1,+0.9]  ≡ t3
    0      -1.4 [-3.3,+0.1] -4.0 [-9.5,+5.6]  -3.1 [-8.9,-0.2]  ≡ t3
    1      -1.7 [-3.5,+0.4] -4.3 [-10.7,+2.8] -3.6 [-9.3,-0.1]  ≡ t3
    2      -2.1 [-4.3,-0.8] -4.6 [-11.6,+4.7] -4.0 [-10.2,-1.0] (old st8: -4.8)
    4      -2.6 [-4.3,-0.5] -4.3 [-10.7,+3.4] -4.5 [-9.7,-0.5]  (old st8: -3.3)
    6      -1.7 [-3.6,-0.4] -6.3 [-11.6,+1.9] -5.8 [-10.2,-0.3] (old st8: -4.9)
    8      -2.0 [-3.8,-1.1] -12.2 [-20.6,-1.5] -4.5 [-12.6,-1.4](old st8: -8.5)
   10      -2.1 [-4.2,-1.2] -14.2 [-22.6,-4.3] -6.1 [-12.3,+0.1](old st8: -11.7)
   12      -2.1 [-4.2,-1.2] -14.2 [-22.6,-4.3] -6.1 [-12.3,+0.1](old st8: -11.7)

WINNER: `t3` / the StillImageTune bundle (byte-identical to it) at every
zone. t4 is within noise of t3 at p-1 (head-to-head 19/19) and p4, and
clearly worse from p6 up. t2 is a consistent small win vs t1 but never
beats t3. IQ's advantage grows with preset speed because its tools
(variance boost, QM, sharpness) survive where the slower presets' heavier
search already captures most of the gain.

Encode cost of the winner vs t1 (median wall / cpu per cell):
   -1: +27% wall, +88% cpu   0: +26% / +10%   1: +16% / -4%
    4: +21% / +137%          6: +18% / -63%   8: +29% / -27%
   10: +30% / -10%          12: +15% / -34%
(Tile-thread scheduling dominates at slow presets — cpu_ms is noisy;
wall_ms is the honest cost: roughly +15-30% for IQ everywhere.)

========================= 3. EXTRAS ABLATION vs plain IQ =================

Round 3 (p4/6/8/10, n=168 per arm pooled) + octile round (3024 cells),
all BD-rate vs `t3` on the SAME corrected metric:

  arm                     BD%med (p4/6/8/10)              verdict
  s3  (sharpness 3)       +1.3/+3.4/+1.9/+1.9            WORSE
  s4  (sharpness 4)       +0.1/ 0.0/-0.4/-0.2            ~neutral (90/168 neg.)
  s5  (sharpness 5)       -0.1/-0.4/-0.4/-0.2            best of grid:
                                                       -0.34% pooled, 100/168
                                                       neg., p≈0.017 — real but
                                                       inside per-image noise
  s6  (sharpness 6)       -0.2/ 0.0/-0.1/-0.1            -0.10% pooled
  ac10 (ac_bias 1.0)      -0.2/-0.0/-0.0/0.0             neutral — not pinned
  cv1 (vb curve 1)        +1.1/+1.0/+1.0/+1.0            WORSE
  qm2/qm6 (min_qm 2/6)    0.00 byte-identical            min_qm doesn't bind
  s0/vs2                  0.00 byte-identical            env=default: absorbed
  o6  (octile 6)          +0.10/-0.17/-0.34/-0.26        within noise
  o7/o7ac                 +0.43/-0.10/+0.53/+0.28        within noise
  o8  (octile 8)          +1.10/+0.57/+1.87/+1.32        WORSE — the old pin
  vb4 (strength 4, r2)    +3.8% bytes matched-qp         WORSE — dropped

Recipe v1 therefore pins NOTHING beyond IQ's own bundle: every measured
extra is neutral or worse at ≥ one zone, and the best of them — sharpness
5, the bottom of the s3>s4>s5>s6>s7 response curve — buys only ~0.3% at
p75 +0.55 (a third of cells still lose). Sharpness is also the one knob
whose whole purpose is trading metric points for edge crispness, so
spending it to win an ssim2 sweep is self-defeating; callers who want it
can set `SVT_FORK_SHARPNESS=5` / `hdr.sharpness = 5` and the recipe will
preserve it. The bundle keeps IQ's 7.

========================= 3b. SB128+VB defect found & fixed =================

The first zone sweep produced `Failed to decode tile data` for EVERY
IQ-family cell at preset -1 (378/378 cells) while C produced clean sb64
streams for the identical config. Root cause: C derives `super_block_size`
in `set_param_based_on_input` AFTER the tune overrides applied in
`copy_api_from_app`, and its rule forces 64 whenever
`enable_variance_boost` is on (enc_handle.c:4077). The port derived
sb_size in `new()` — before `hdr` mutations existed — so tune IQ kept the
sb128 the -1 preset wants, then emitted per-64 delta-q symbols inside an
sb128 tile: decoder desync.

Fix (this change): `encode_frame_impl` re-derives `sb_size` immediately
after the tune-override application point (moved to match C ordering);
the delta-q emission gate uses the real `sb_size` instead of a hardcoded
64; the VB plan is truncated to `sb_total_count` mirroring C's
`variance[sb_addr]`-over-b64-map quirk. Results: all p-1/p0/p1 IQ cells
decode (6930/6930 cells clean); auto-derived ≡ explicit `SVTAV1_SB=64`
byte-identical; VB-off cells byte-identical to pre-fix; forced
`SVTAV1_SB=128`+VB (a port extension C cannot express) now emits a
decodable stream rather than a corrupt one.

========================= 4. CAVEATS =========================

- **Parser bug invalidated the first read.** The y4m→I420 converter sliced
  frame bytes before skipping the `FRAME\n` marker (6-byte shift per
  frame). Byte counts (read from the .obu) were unaffected, but every
  decoded image was corrupted and ssim2 ran deep negative — the earlier
  "oct8 = -13% bytes at Δssim2≈0, 108/0" headline measured a broken
  reference. With the corrected parser the stone-texture cell scores
  79.98 at q20 (was -471) and BD-rate is computable; the oct8 pin was
  actually +0.6..+1.9% WORSE than plain IQ and was dropped.
- BD-rate is piecewise-linear log-rate on 3 qp points, integrated over
  the overlapping quality range — robust to the non-monotone flat-content
  curves that made cubic BD explode earlier (renders +222% artifact).
- Matched-qp bytes still mislead here: IQ buys +9..+12 ssim2 for +33%
  bytes at q20 — at fixed qp it looks expensive; on the rate-quality
  curve it wins at every zone. The honest baseline row is the BD table,
  not matched-qp bytes.
- wall_ms includes process spawn + PNG decode (~0.3s floor); cpu_ms is
  child rusage user+sys (tile-parallel at slow presets → cpu >> wall).
- n=2 per class: per-class rows are indicative; pooled medians + win/loss
  counts are the claim.
- s0/vs2 arms are vacuous by construction: an env-set value equal to the
  mode default is indistinguishable from unset, so the recipe correctly
  leaves IQ's value in place — they verify byte-identity, not the knob.
